From 2b007d22c12bf7c117c12ff11eecdb1518eb4a0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek <abhishek01789@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:45:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/41] Lamp on open, hold tiles while minimizing, act on
 Window View cards

- Magic Lamp also pours a new window out of its taskbar icon; it waits up
  to 300 ms for plasmashell to lay the icon out
- Minimizing holds the tile layout until the lamp ends, and the lamp draws
  above other windows and fullscreen, under the panel
- Lamp frames are capped at 1/30 s so a stall slows it instead of skipping
- The Window View uses the Alt+Tab backdrop and white glow (shared code)
- The hovered card shows its traffic lights: minimize pours the card into
  the taskbar and keeps it dimmed, maximize maximizes and switches, close
  closes and the other cards make room; middle click closes
- Off-screen windows fade in and out at their cell instead of sliding
- debug.magicLamp and debug.windowViewPointer IPC for tests
